      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 93,
      "bottomRightX": 676,
      "bottomRightY": 131,
      "content": "We examine the asymptotic behavior of the solution at infinity. In order to get a simple relationship, we assume that $V(x)$ vanishes faster than $x^{-2}$ at infinity; i.e.:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 326,
      "topLeftY": 148,
      "bottomRightX": 676,
      "bottomRightY": 185,
      "content": "$$| V(x) | < \\frac{K}{x^2}, \\tag{4}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 204,
      "bottomRightX": 339,
      "bottomRightY": 223,
      "content": "in which $K$ is a positive number ($^1$).",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 135,
      "topLeftY": 224,
      "bottomRightX": 472,
      "bottomRightY": 243,
      "content": "We now determine $\\psi(x)$ by a process of iteration; let:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 327,
      "topLeftY": 258,
      "bottomRightX": 676,
      "bottomRightY": 280,
      "content": "$$u_0(x) = e^{ikx}, \\tag{5}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 297,
      "bottomRightX": 569,
      "bottomRightY": 315,
      "content": "and let $u_1(x), u_2(x), \\ldots$ be the solutions of the successive approximations:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 322,
      "topLeftY": 334,
      "bottomRightX": 469,
      "bottomRightY": 374,
      "content": "$$\\frac{d^2 u_n}{dx^2} + k^2 u_n = V u_{n-1},$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 376,
      "bottomRightX": 291,
      "bottomRightY": 392,
      "content": "which vanishes as $x \\to +\\infty$.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 136,
      "topLeftY": 394,
      "bottomRightX": 226,
      "bottomRightY": 410,
      "content": "One then has:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 264,
      "topLeftY": 413,
      "bottomRightX": 522,
      "bottomRightY": 450,
      "content": "$$u_n(x) = \\frac{1}{k} \\int_x^\\infty u_{n-1}(\\xi) V(\\xi) \\sin k(\\xi - x) d\\xi,$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 470,
      "bottomRightX": 341,
      "bottomRightY": 488,
      "content": "as one can verify directly. One has:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 280,
      "topLeftY": 507,
      "bottomRightX": 507,
      "bottomRightY": 543,
      "content": "$$| u_n(x) | \\le \\frac{1}{k} \\int_x^\\infty | u_{n-1}(\\xi) | \\cdot | V(\\xi) | d\\xi.$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 545,
      "bottomRightX": 238,
      "bottomRightY": 561,
      "content": "We now show that:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 329,
      "topLeftY": 565,
      "bottomRightX": 458,
      "bottomRightY": 608,
      "content": "$$| u_n(x) | \\le \\frac{1}{n!} \\left( \\frac{K}{kx} \\right)^n.$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 111,
      "topLeftY": 629,
      "bottomRightX": 676,
      "bottomRightY": 664,
      "content": "This is correct for $n = 0$, since it follows from (5) that $| u_0(x) | \\le 1$. We now assume that is it correct for $n - 1$:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 304,
      "topLeftY": 667,
      "bottomRightX": 484,
      "bottomRightY": 714,
      "content": "$$| u_{n-1}(\\xi) | \\le \\frac{1}{(n-1)!} \\left( \\frac{K}{k\\xi} \\right)^{n-1};$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 716,
      "bottomRightX": 238,
      "bottomRightY": 731,
      "content": "it then follows that:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 218,
      "topLeftY": 734,
      "bottomRightX": 569,
      "bottomRightY": 780,
      "content": "$$| u_n(x) | \\le \\frac{1}{k} \\frac{1}{(n-1)!} \\left( \\frac{K}{k} \\right)^{n-1} \\cdot K \\int_x^\\infty \\xi^{-n+1} \\xi^2 d\\xi = \\frac{1}{n!} \\left( \\frac{K}{kx} \\right)^n,$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "equation"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 112,
      "topLeftY": 782,
      "bottomRightX": 216,
      "bottomRightY": 797,
      "content": "as was asserted.",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 136,
      "topLeftY": 800,
      "bottomRightX": 277,
      "bottomRightY": 816,
      "content": "As a result, the series:",
      "confidenceScores": null,
      "type": "text"
    },
    {
      "topLeftX": 329,
      "topLeftY": 819,
      "bottomRightX": 676,
      "bottomRightY": 859,
      "content": "$$\\psi(x) = \\sum_{n=0}^\\infty u_n(x) \\tag{6}$$",
      "confidenceScores": null,
